.TH "SKARN-CHECK" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.17.0" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-check \- Scan AI sessions for leaked credentials and attack patterns
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBcheck\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan AI sessions for leaked credentials and attack patterns.
.PP
Control the security scan: which rules run, the scan window, output format,
and CI gating.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rules\fR \fIpath\fR
Load a custom TOML rules file in addition to the bundled rules.
.TP
\fB\-\-ai\-rules\fR \fIpath\fR
Load an AI\-specific rules file.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ai\-rules\fR
Disable the AI\-specific rules.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-default\-rules\fR
Disable the bundled detection rules.
.TP
\fB\-\-feed\fR \fIpath\fR
Apply a signed maintained\-feed bundle over the baseline rules. Requires a
Team license.
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-rules\fR
Fetch and verify the latest feed from the subscriber channel, then scan.
Requires a Team license.
.TP
\fB\-\-feed\-url\fR \fIurl\fR
Feed channel URL for \-\-update\-rules; falls back to $SKARN_FEED_URL.
Requires a Team license.
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Disable all network access (the maintained\-feed fetch).
.TP
\fB\-\-severity\fR \fIlevel\fR
Report only findings at or above this severity. One of: low, medium, high,
critical. The default is medium.
.TP
\fB\-\-canary\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
File of planted canary tokens, one per line; a match is a proven breach.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-packages\fR
Flag typosquatted or URL\-sourced package installs found in sessions
(offline).
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-code\fR
Flag insecure code written by the assistant during the session.
.TP
\fB\-\-hours\fR \fIn\fR
Scan window in hours; 0 means no time limit. The default is 720.
.TP
\fB\-\-cli\fR \fIname\fR
Restrict the scan to one assistant's sessions. One of: claude, gemini, codex,
cursor, copilot.
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIpath\fR
Restrict the scan to sessions under this project path.
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fIid\fR
Scan a single session by id.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format. ndjson is an ECS\-shaped event stream (one redacted finding per
line) for SIEM ingest. One of: text, json, sarif, ndjson. The default is text.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-redact\fR
Show secrets in full instead of redacting them. Use with caution.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colored output.
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fIpath\fR
Load a declarative TOML policy file (fail thresholds, required/forbidden
rules, baseline enforcement, profile); the \-\-fail\-on\-* and \-\-profile
flags override it. Requires a Team license.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIpreset\fR
Output profile. enterprise keeps high\-confidence findings and dedups them.
One of: enterprise. Requires an Enterprise license.
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-severity\fR \fIlevel\fR
Exit 1 if any finding is at or above this severity. One of: low, medium, high,
critical.
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-risk\fR \fI0\-100\fR
Exit 2 if the session risk score exceeds this threshold.
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-scan\-error\fR
Fail closed (exit 6) when the scan was incomplete: a tool source errored out
of discovery, or a session's parse failed. Off by default (a partial scan
still reports, with a stderr warning).
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\fR \fIpath\fR
Suppress findings recorded in this baseline; fail only on new findings. A
single file is free; a directory unions every .json baseline inside it (an
org\-shared accepted set) and requires a Team license. Without this flag,
~/.config/skarn/baseline.json is applied automatically when it exists
(suppression only; \-\-baseline\-create and \-\-baseline\-merge targets stay
explicit).
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\-create\fR
Write the current findings to the \-\-baseline file as the accepted set and
exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-baseline\-merge\fR \fIfile\fR
Consolidate the \-\-baseline input (a file or a directory of per\-member
baselines) into one distributable file and exit. Requires a Team license.
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-log\fR \fIfile\fR
Append a hash\-chained record of this scan (timestamp, policy, finding counts,
verdict; no secrets) to this local log; detects in\-place edits and reordering
of recorded history. Requires a Team license.
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-verify\fR \fIfile\fR
Verify an audit log's hash chain and exit (no scan). Exits non\-zero if the
chain is broken. Needs no license.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Clean, or informational output only.
.TP
\fB1\fR
A finding at or above the \-\-fail\-on\-severity threshold was reported. For
setup and guard \-\-self\-test: a target was refused or a verification failed.
For doctor: at least one check FAILED (a warning never exits nonzero, and
\-\-json always exits 0).
.TP
\fB2\fR
The session risk score exceeded the \-\-fail\-on\-risk threshold. For setup:
no terminal to prompt on and no \-\-yes; the exact non\-interactive command is
printed.
.TP
\fB3\fR
A canary token was triggered (a proven breach). This overrides every other
gate.
.TP
\fB4\fR
A policy precondition was not met: a required rule is missing, or the policy
requires a baseline and none was supplied.
.TP
\fB5\fR
A requested paid feature is not covered by the license (a Team or Enterprise
flag without a matching license). Refused before any scan; the free core does
not exit 5.
.TP
\fB6\fR
The scan could not complete: session discovery or the scan itself failed.
Fail\-closed \- the result is not trustworthy, so it is never reported as
clean.
.SH SECURITY
Skarn scans locally and makes no network connection by default. Secrets are
redacted in every output format unless \-\-no\-redact is given.
.PP
The only feature that transmits anything off the machine is the maintained
feed: \-\-update\-rules and \-\-feed\-url fetch a signed feed bundle from the
subscriber channel. No secret ever leaves the machine. It is off by default
and is disabled by \-\-offline.
